    "text": "Definition Of Forensic Medicine.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Legal System & Medical Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Definition of Forensic Medicine and Medical Jurisprudence\n\n**Forensic Medicine** (also known as Legal Medicine) is the specialized branch of medical science that deals with the application of medical knowledge, principles, and clinical skills to the administration of law and the delivery of justice, both in civil and criminal matters. It primarily involves post-mortem examinations, injury assessment, and clinical forensic evaluations.\n\nIn contrast, **Medical Jurisprudence** deals with the legal aspects of medical practice. It encompasses the study of the rights, duties, ethical obligations, privileges, and legal liabilities of a registered medical practitioner in relation to patients, professional colleagues, and the State (such as consent, medical negligence, and professional misconduct).",
