    "text": "Differences between civil and criminal negligence.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Medical Law & Ethics",
    "answer": "### Differences between Civil and Criminal Negligence\n\n| Feature | Civil Negligence | Criminal Negligence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Standard of Proof** | Established by a **preponderance of probabilities**. | Must be proved **beyond a reasonable doubt**. |\n| **Liability / Penalty** | The doctor is held civilly liable to pay **financial compensation** to the patient. | The doctor faces **criminal punishment**, including imprisonment and/or a fine. |\n| **Degree of Negligence** | Involves a lack of ordinary care, minor errors, or omission of standard skill. | Involves **gross, reckless, and wanton disregard** for human life and safety. |\n| **Legal Forum** | Tried in Civil Courts or Consumer Disputes Redressal Forums. | Tried in Criminal Courts of Law (under **Section 106 BNS** / 304A IPC). |",
