    "answer": "### Professional Secret: Definition and Scope\n\nA **Professional Secret** (or Professional Confidentiality) refers to all confidential personal and clinical information regarding a patient's diagnosis, medical history, test results, and private life that a registered medical practitioner acquires during the course of their professional relationship.\n\n**Ethical Foundation**:\nThe duty to preserve professional secrets is a cornerstone of the doctor-patient relationship, historically rooted in the Hippocratic Oath. A patient shares sensitive information expecting it will not be shared with others.\n\n**Breach**:\nDivulging a professional secret without the patient's explicit consent constitutes professional misconduct. The only exceptions are when disclosure is legally mandated, ordered by a court of law, or falls under **Privileged Communication** to protect public safety.",
