    "text": "Add A Note On BITE MARKS & It's MLI.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Forensic Thanatology & Identity",
    "answer": "### Definition and Nature of Bite Marks\n\nA **Bite Mark** is a physical pattern or injury left on a surface, most commonly human skin or food items (such as apples, cheese, or chocolate), by the teeth of a human or an animal. Human bite marks typically present as a circular or elliptical injury, consisting of two opposing U-shaped arches (representing the maxilla and mandible) separated by a space.\n\nThe severity of a bite mark ranges from superficial bruising and abrasions to deep lacerations, puncture wounds, and complete tissue avulsion.\n\n---\n\n### Forensic Collection and Analysis of Bite Marks\n\nThe forensic protocol for analyzing bite marks must be executed quickly before tissue distortion or healing occurs:\n*   **Documentation**: Immediate photography of the bite mark at a right angle using a standard forensic scale (such as the ABFO No. 2 scale) is mandatory to prevent perspective distortion.\n*   **Saliva Swabbing**: Swabbing the bite site with a sterile cotton swab to collect saliva. This provides cellular material for DNA profiling of the perpetrator.\n*   **Casting and Comparison**: Taking dental impressions of the suspect's dentition to create stone models. These models are compared with the bite mark using transparent overlays or 3D digital scanning.\n\n---\n\n### Medico-Legal Importance (MLI)\n\n*   **Association with Specific Crimes**: Bite marks are frequently encountered in violent crimes, particularly sexual assault (found on breasts, neck, thighs), child abuse (found on buttocks, abdomen), and homicides.\n*   **Offensive vs. Defensive Bites**:\n    *   *Offensive bites* are inflicted by the perpetrator on the victim to control or torture them.\n    *   *Defensive bites* are inflicted by the victim on the hands, forearms, or chest of the attacker during a struggle, linking the suspect directly to the victim.\n*   **Unique Dental Profiling**: Every individual has unique dental characteristics, such as missing teeth, overcrowding, gaps (diastema), and chips, which can positively identify or exclude a suspect.",
