    "text": "Write About  Cephalic Index And Its Types.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Forensic Thanatology & Identity",
    "answer": "### Cephalic Index: Definition and Classification\n\nThe **Cephalic Index** (referred to as the Cranial Index when measured directly on dry skulls) is an anthropometric ratio used to describe the shape of the human head.\n\n**Formula**:\n$$\text{Cephalic Index} = \frac{\text{Maximum Breadth of Head}}{\text{Maximum Length of Head}} \times 100$$\n\n**Types/Classification**:\nBased on the Cephalic Index, human heads are classified into three primary categories:\n1.  **Dolichocephalic (Long-headed)**: Index $\\le 75$. Characteristic of Aryans, Dravidians, and African races.\n2.  **Mesocephalic (Medium-headed)**: Index $75.1$ to $79.9$. Characteristic of European and Chinese populations.\n3.  **Brachycephalic (Short/Round-headed)**: Index $\\ge 80$. Characteristic of Mongolians and Native Americans.\n\n**Medico-Legal Importance**:\nIt is valuable in forensic anthropology to help determine the race and ethnic origin of unidentified skeletal remains.",
