    "id": 47,
    "text": "Add a note on objectives of Medico Legal Autopsy.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Medico-Legal Autopsy",
    "answer": "### Objectives of Medico-Legal Autopsy\n\nA medico-legal autopsy (postmortem examination) is performed under legal authority to investigate sudden, suspicious, unnatural, or unexplained deaths. Its primary objectives are:\n\n1. **Establish Identity**: To identify the deceased when the body is unknown or highly decomposed.\n2. **Determine Cause of Death**: To find the exact anatomical and physiological cause of death (e.g., hemorrhage, asphyxia, poisoning).\n3. **Determine Manner of Death**: To help distinguish whether the death was suicidal, homicidal, accidental, or natural.\n4. **Estimate Time Since Death**: To determine the postmortem interval (TSD) based on postmortem changes.\n5. **Document and Interpret Injuries**: To record the nature, age, size, and direction of wounds and determine if they are ante-mortem or postmortem.\n6. **Collect Trace Evidence**: To recover foreign materials (bullets, fibers, semen, hair, poisons) for forensic analysis.",
