    "id": 55,
    "text": "Add a note on BRAIN STEM DEATH",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Thanatology",
    "answer": "### Brain Stem Death\n\n**Definition**\nBrain stem death is defined as the complete, permanent, and irreversible loss of function of the brain stem. Because the brain stem contains vital centers controlling cardiovascular reflexes and spontaneous respiration, its death equates to the legal death of the individual, even if cardiac action is temporarily maintained artificially by a ventilator.\n\n**Clinical Criteria for Declaration**\nUnder the **Transplantation of Human Organs and Tissues Act (THOTA), 2014**, brain stem death must be certified by a board of four medical practitioners (including a neurologist/neurosurgeon and the hospital superintendent) using the following strict protocol, performed twice with a minimum interval of 6 hours:\n\n1. **Prerequisites**:\n   * The patient must be in a deep, irreversible coma of known etiology (e.g., severe traumatic brain injury, massive intracranial hemorrhage).\n   * Reversible causes of coma (hypothermia, drug intoxication, neuromuscular blockades, severe metabolic/endocrine disorders) must be ruled out.\n2. **Absence of Brain Stem Reflexes**:\n   * *Pupillary Reflex*: Pupils are fixed, dilated, and non-reactive to light.\n   * *Corneal Reflex*: Absent bilaterally.\n   * *Oculo-vestibular (Caloric) Reflex*: No eye movement when $50 \\text{ ml}$ of ice-cold water is irrigated into the external auditory canal.\n   * *Oculo-cephalic (Doll's Eye) Reflex*: Eyes move passively with the head.\n   * *Gag and Cough Reflexes*: Absent during pharyngeal stimulation and tracheal suctioning.\n3. **Apnea Test**:\n   * This is the definitive test to confirm the absence of spontaneous respiration.\n   * The ventilator is disconnected while oxygenating the patient with $100\\% \\text{ O}_2$ via a catheter. The arterial carbon dioxide level ($PaCO_2$) is allowed to rise above $60 \\text{ mmHg}$ (or $20 \\text{ mmHg}$ above baseline). If no respiratory effort is observed, the apnea test is positive, indicating brain stem death.\n\n**Medico-Legal Importance**\nBrain stem death certification is essential for the legal harvesting of viable organs (kidneys, liver, heart) for transplantation.",
