    "answer": "### Syncope\n\n**Syncope** is a mode of somatic death starting from the failure of the heart (circulatory system). It is characterized by the sudden and complete cessation of the heart's action, leading to cerebral ischemia, immediate loss of consciousness, and death if circulation is not restored.\n\n**Common Causes:**\n* Massive hemorrhage (external or internal).\n* Sudden emotional shock or intense pain.\n* Reflex vagal inhibition (due to stimulation of the carotid sinus or laryngeal nerves).\n* Myocardial infarction or sudden cardiac arrest.\n* Valvular heart disease or severe myocarditis.\n\n**Postmortem Findings:**\n* The heart is typically contracted and empty of blood (if death is instantaneous) or flaccid with blood in all chambers.\n* General pallor of the internal organs (viscera) if death was caused by acute hemorrhage.\n* Minimal congestion, unlike in asphyxial deaths.",
