    "text": "Suspended Animation",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Thanatology",
    "answer": "### Suspended Animation\n\n**Suspended Animation**, also known as **apparent death**, is a state in which the vital functions of the body (respiration, circulation, and brain activity) are reduced to such a low level that they cannot be detected by ordinary clinical examinations, though life is not entirely extinct.\n\n**Common Causes:**\n* Hypothermia or apparent drowning in freezing water.\n* Barbiturate, opiate, or anesthetic overdose.\n* Electrocution or lightning strike.\n* Asphyxia in newborns.\n* Voluntary yogic meditation (Samadhi).\n\n**Medico-Legal Importance:**\nA person in suspended animation may be mistakenly declared dead, leading to premature burial or autopsy. Therefore, life must be confirmed using sensitive diagnostic tests (e.g., ECG, EEG, ophthalmoscopic examination showing segmented blood flow in retinal vessels) before certifying death.",
