    "text": "Medical Legal Importance Of Lucid Interval.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Forensic Psychiatry",
    "answer": "### Medico-Legal Importance of a Lucid Interval\n\n**Definition:**\nA **lucid interval** is a temporary period of sanity and mental clarity in a mentally ill person, or a temporary period of consciousness following a head injury (concussion) before the onset of coma.\n\n**Medico-Legal Importance (MLI):**\n1. **Testamentary Capacity**: A mentally ill person can execute a legally valid and binding Will during a certified lucid interval.\n2. **Contracts and Marriage**: They are legally capable of entering into binding business contracts, buying or selling property, and marrying during this period.\n3. **Criminal Liability**: If a person commits a crime during a lucid interval, they are held fully criminally responsible and cannot claim the defense of insanity under Section 84 IPC.\n4. **Head Injuries**: In trauma, a lucid interval is classically seen in extradural hemorrhage (EDH), representing a critical window for surgical intervention before fatal brain compression occurs.",
