    "id": 83,
    "text": "Write About TESTAMENTARY CAPACITY. What Is Holographic Will?",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Forensic Psychiatry",
    "answer": "### Testamentary Capacity and Holographic Will\n\n**Testamentary Capacity**\nTestamentary capacity refers to the legal ability of a person (the testator) to make a valid, legally binding Will. To possess a **\"sound disposing mind,\"** the testator must:\n1. Understand the nature and consequences of making a Will.\n2. Understand the extent and character of the property they are disposing of.\n3. Recognize the natural beneficiaries (relatives) and their claims.\nA medical practitioner must examine the testator and certify their soundness of mind at the exact time the Will is signed.\n\n**Holographic Will**\nA holographic Will is a Will written **entirely in the testator's own handwriting**, signed and dated by them. It does not strictly require formal witnesses in some jurisdictions, though it carries high legal weight because forging an entire handwritten document is exceptionally difficult.",
