    "id": 123,
    "text": "Write About Various Types Of Torture Methods.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Medico-Legal Aspects of Wounds",
    "answer": "Torture is the deliberate, systematic infliction of severe physical or mental pain by state or non-state actors. The Istanbul Protocol guidelines govern the documentation of such injuries.\n\n### Physical Torture Methods\n1.  **Beating and Blunt Force**:\n    *   *Falanga (Falaka)*: Repeated beating of the soles of the feet with rods or whips. It causes severe soft-tissue injury, compartmental syndrome, and chronic foot pain without visible external scars.\n    *   *Telephono*: Slapping both ears simultaneously, causing tympanic membrane rupture and middle ear damage.\n2.  **Positional Torture**:\n    *   *Suspension (e.g., Palestine Hanging)*: Suspending the victim by the wrists tied behind their back, causing shoulder dislocation and brachial plexus injury.\n3.  **Thermal and Electrical Torture**:\n    *   *Electroshock (e.g., Picana)*: Application of electric currents to sensitive areas (genitals, breasts), causing minute circular burns or metallic deposition on skin.\n    *   *Cigarette Burns*: Characteristic circular, deep, punched-out third-degree burns.\n4.  **Asphyxiation Methods**:\n    *   *Wet Submarino*: Submerging the head in contaminated water containing feces or vomit to simulate drowning.\n    *   *Dry Submarino*: Placing a plastic bag over the head until near-suffocation.\n\n---\n\n### Medico-Legal Importance\nThe forensic pathologist must document physical scars, perform radiological imaging of deep tissues, and correlate the findings with the victim's testimony to prove human rights violations and bring the perpetrators to justice.",
