    "text": "Gagging                                             B)Choking& It's Management",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Mechanical Asphyxia",
    "answer": "### A) Gagging\nGagging is a form of mechanical suffocation where the mouth is tightly obstructed using a cloth, paper, adhesive tape, or rubber ball. This forces the tongue backward against the pharynx, blocking the airway. If the nostrils are also covered, or if nasal secretions block the nose, death occurs rapidly due to asphyxia.\n\n---\n\n### B) Choking & Its Management\nChoking is the mechanical obstruction of the internal air passages (larynx or trachea) by a foreign body like a food bolus, coin, or seed.\n\n#### Emergency Management:\n1.  **Heimlich Maneuver:** Give rapid upward abdominal thrusts to force the diaphragm up and expel the object.\n2.  **Back Blows & Chest Thrusts:** In infants, administer 5 back blows followed by 5 chest thrusts.\n3.  **Magill Forceps:** Used under direct laryngoscopy to extract visible foreign bodies.\n4.  **Cricothyroidotomy:** An emergency surgical airway created if complete obstruction cannot be cleared immediately.",
