    "answer": "### Death due to Starvation and Neglect\n\n**Starvation** is the deprivation of food and water essential to maintain life.\n\n#### Clinical Features:\nExtreme emaciation, loose wrinkled skin due to loss of subcutaneous fat, sunken eyes, hollow cheeks, prominent ribs, scaphoid abdomen, bradycardia, hypothermia, and severe lethargy.\n\n#### Postmortem Findings:\n1.  **External:** Skeletal appearance, prominent bones, dry parchment-like skin, and bedsores.\n2.  **Internal:** Atrophy of all organs (except the brain and heart). The stomach and intestines are paper-thin, translucent, and completely empty. The gallbladder is distended with thick, dark-green bile.\n\n#### Medicolegal Importance (MLI):\n1.  **Homicidal:** Mostly seen in the neglect or deliberate starvation of infants, step-children, disabled individuals, or the elderly by caregivers.\n2.  **Suicidal:** Voluntary hunger strikes (e.g., in prisoners) or anorexia nervosa.\n3.  **Accidental:** Famines, shipwrecks, or being trapped in mines. The pathologist must rule out natural wasting diseases (e.g., cancer, tuberculosis, AIDS).",
