    "text": "Super-Foecundationand Super-Foetation.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Superfecundation and Superfetation\n\n#### Superfecundation:\n**Superfecundation** is the fertilization of two or more ova liberated during the same menstrual cycle by sperm from separate acts of coitus, either by the same man or by two different men, within a short timeframe. \n*   **Medicolegal Significance:** This can result in twins with different biological fathers (heteropaternal superfecundation), which is definitively proven using DNA profiling in cases of disputed paternity.\n\n---\n\n### Superfetation:\n**Superfetation** is the fertilization of a second ovum liberated from an ovary during an active, ongoing pregnancy, resulting in the development of two fetuses of different gestational ages within the same uterus.\n*   **Mechanism:** It is extremely rare in humans because the hormonal changes of pregnancy actively suppress ovulation and menstruation.\n*   **Medicolegal Significance:** Twins are born at the same time but display distinct physical maturity and birth weights, raising questions about gestation and paternity.",
