    "text": "Two finger test OR Virgin Test.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Two-Finger Test (Virgin Test)\n\nThe **two-finger test** is an archaic gynecological practice where a clinician inserts two fingers into a woman’s vagina to assess vaginal laxity, the integrity of the hymen, and the tone of the pelvic muscles to determine if she is a virgin or has been sexually active.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Status and Scientific Invalidity:\n1.  **Strictly Banned:** The Supreme Court of India has declared the two-finger test illegal, unscientific, and a grave violation of a woman's right to privacy, dignity, and bodily integrity. It is strictly prohibited in the examination of rape survivors.\n2.  **No Scientific Value:** Vaginal laxity and hymeneal distensibility vary widely due to anatomical factors, sports, and tampon use, and do not correlate with a history of sexual intercourse.\n3.  **Professional Misconduct:** Performing this test now constitutes professional misconduct and is a punishable offense under the law.",
