    "text": "Surrogate motherhood",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Surrogate Motherhood\n\n**Surrogate motherhood** is an arrangement where a woman (the surrogate) agrees to carry a pregnancy to term and give birth to a child for another couple or individual (the commissioning or intended parents), with the legal agreement to hand over the child after birth.\n\n---\n\n### Types:\n1.  **Gestational (Host) Surrogacy:** The surrogate has no genetic connection to the child. The embryo is created via IVF using the intended parents' or donors' gametes and transferred to the surrogate's uterus.\n2.  **Traditional Surrogacy:** The surrogate's own egg is fertilized by the intended father's or donor's sperm, making her genetically related to the child.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Aspects:\nIn India, surrogacy is governed by the **Surrogacy (Regulation) Act, 2021**. The law strictly bans commercial surrogacy and permits only altruistic surrogacy (reimbursing only medical expenses). It ensures the child is legally recognized as the legitimate child of the commissioning parents.",
