    "text": "Section 416 CRPC .",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Section 416 CRPC\n\n**Section 416 of the Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC), 1973** (in India), deals with the postponement or commutation of a death sentence in the case of a pregnant woman.\n\n---\n\n### Key Provisions:\n*   If a woman sentenced to death is found to be pregnant, the High Court **shall** order the execution of the sentence to be postponed.\n*   The High Court may also, if it thinks fit, commute the death sentence to imprisonment for life.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Significance:\nThis statutory provision is based on humanitarian grounds to protect the innocent unborn child from being executed alongside the mother. \n\nThe forensic pathologist or authorized medical officer plays a critical role under this section. They must perform clinical, biochemical, and radiological examinations (ultrasound) to definitively diagnose the pregnancy and submit an official report to the court to initiate the stay of execution.",
