    "text": "ATAVISM.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Atavism\n\n**Atavism** (also known as evolutionary throwback) is the reappearance of an ancestral genetic trait or physical characteristic in an organism after several generations of absence, which is not present in its immediate parents.\n\n---\n\n### Mechanism:\nIt occurs due to the reactivation of dormant, silent genes that were suppressed during evolutionary history but remained preserved in the DNA.\n\n---\n\n### Examples in Humans:\n*   Babies born with a vestigial tail.\n*   Extreme body hair (hypertrichosis/werewolf syndrome).\n*   Extra nipples (polymastia).\n*   Large canine teeth.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Significance:\nAtavistic traits can create sudden doubts about paternity or legitimacy, as the child exhibits physical anomalies absent in both parents. \n\nThe forensic specialist must distinguish these benign evolutionary throwbacks from congenital malformations caused by maternal trauma, drug abuse, or teratogens during pregnancy in medical negligence suits.",
