    "text": "Suppositious children.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Suppositious Children\n\nA **suppositious child** is a child who is fraudulently presented by a woman as her own biological offspring when, in reality, she did not give birth to it. \n\n---\n\n### Motives:\nThis fraud is typically committed to secure an inheritance, claim maintenance, prevent a divorce, or keep a husband.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Investigation:\n1.  **Examination of the Alleged Mother:** The forensic expert examines the woman for signs of recent pregnancy and delivery (breast changes, uterine involution, vaginal laxity, and lochia). If she shows no signs of recent delivery, the claim is discredited.\n2.  **DNA Profiling:** The gold standard. DNA parentage testing of the child, the alleged mother, and the alleged father will definitively confirm or exclude biological maternity and paternity.\n3.  **Legal Action:** Suppositious child cases involve criminal offenses of cheating, fraud, and impersonation under the law.",
