    "id": 172,
    "text": "Precipitate labour",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Jurisprudence",
    "answer": "### Precipitate Labour\n\n**Precipitate labor** is an unusually rapid, sudden childbirth where the combined stages of labor last for less than three hours.\n\n---\n\n### Predisposing Factors:\nMultiparity, unusually strong uterine contractions, a spacious pelvis, small fetal size, or lax perineal muscles.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Importance:\n\n#### 1. Infanticide vs. Accidental Death\nA child may be born suddenly while the mother is standing or using the toilet. The child may fall, sustaining head injuries (e.g., parietal fractures) or drown in the toilet. This can mimic homicidal infanticide.\n*   **Differentiating Feature:** In precipitate labor, the umbilical cord is torn or ragged rather than cut cleanly, and there are no signs of deliberate violence on the baby.\n\n#### 2. Legal Defense\nThe suddenness of precipitate labor serves as a valid legal defense for the mother against charges of abandoning or exposing the child at birth.",
