    "id": 176,
    "text": "Write About SODOMY. Procedure Of Examination Of Victim Of Sodomy & its MLI",
    "type": "LAQ",
    "chapter": "Sexual Offences",
    "answer": "### Definition of Sodomy\n**Sodomy** (specifically anal intercourse) is historically defined as a form of unnatural sexual offense involving carnal intercourse against the order of nature. In India, it was prosecuted under Section 377 IPC. \n\nFollowing the landmark Supreme Court judgment in *Navtej Singh Johar v. Union of India (2018)*, consensual anal intercourse between adults was decriminalized. However, **non-consensual sodomy** remains a serious criminal offense under the law, prosecuted under modified provisions of rape and assault.\n\n---\n\n### Procedure of Examination of a Victim of Sodomy\n\nThe medical examination of the victim must be systematic, documenting both general bodily injuries and specific localized anal trauma:\n\n#### 1. Consent and History\nObtain informed written consent. Record a detailed history, noting the time of the incident, whether the victim has passed stools, bathed, or washed the anal area since the assault, and if any lubricant was used.\n\n#### 2. Clothing and General Physical Examination\nInspect the victim's clothes for semen, blood, fecal staining, or mud. Perform a complete general physical examination to document any signs of struggle, defense wounds on the hands, or injuries on the buttocks and thighs.\n\n#### 3. Local Anal Examination\nPlace the victim in the **Sims' (lateral recumbent) position** or **knee-chest position** under good lighting. The examination features differ significantly based on whether the victim is accustomed to the act:\n\n##### A. Acute / Occasional Cases (Forceful Sodomy)\n*   **Tenderness and Spasm:** Severe pain and sphincter spasm.\n*   **Injuries:** Abrasions, lacerations, or radial tears in the perianal skin.\n*   **Bleeding:** Active oozing of blood from the tears.\n*   **Swabbing:** Collect anal swabs immediately to detect semen and spermatozoa.\n\n##### B. Chronic / Habitual Cases (Passive Agents)\n*   **Funnel-Shaped Anus:** The anus becomes infundibuliform (funnel-shaped) due to the loss of perianal fat.\n*   **Smooth Skin:** Normal radial skin folds around the anus are flattened or lost.\n*   **Lax Sphincter:** The anal sphincter becomes highly relaxed, offering no resistance, and may patulously dilate when the buttocks are separated.\n*   **Scars:** Healed scars of old lacerations may be visible.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Importance (MLI) of Sodomy\n1.  **Proving Non-Consensual Acts:** Localized lacerations, sphincter spasms, and general bodily bruises provide objective evidence of force and lack of consent.\n2.  **Perpetrator Identification:** The recovery of semen and male DNA from the perianal skin or anal canal is crucial for identifying the accused.\n3.  **Distinguishing Medical Pathology:** The examiner must distinguish genuine sodomy-related lacerations from pre-existing medical conditions like anal fissures, hemorrhoids, or rectal prolapse.",
