    "answer": "### Statutory Rape\n\n**Statutory rape** is a legal term that refers to sexual intercourse with a person who is below the legally defined age of consent, regardless of whether the sexual act was consensual or if force was used.\n\n---\n\n### Legal Context in India:\nUnder Section 375 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC), the age of consent is **18 years**. Therefore, any sexual intercourse by a man with a girl under 18 years of age legally constitutes rape, even if she fully consented to the act and there are no signs of physical violence.\n\n---\n\n### Medicolegal Significance:\n1.  **Consent is Invalid:** The victim's consent is legally null and void, and cannot be used as a defense by the accused.\n2.  **Age Determination:** The primary duty of the forensic medical examiner in these cases is to estimate the exact age of the victim using clinical, dental, and radiological methods (skeletal ossification tests) to prove if she was a minor at the time of the offense.",
