    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Abortion",
    "answer": "### Medical Termination of Pregnancy (Amendment) Act, 2021\nThe MTP Act, 2021 amended the original 1971 Act to expand access to safe and legal abortion:\n- **Gestational Limits & Opinions**:\n  - *Up to 20 weeks*: Requires opinion of one Registered Medical Practitioner (RMP).\n  - *20 to 24 weeks*: Allowed for special categories of women (survivors of sexual assault, rape, incest, minors, disabled, change in marital status during pregnancy), requiring opinion of two RMPs.\n  - *Beyond 24 weeks*: Allowed only for substantial fetal abnormalities diagnosed by a state-level Medical Board.\n\n### Indications for MTP\n1. **Therapeutic**: Risk to the life or grave injury to the physical or mental health of the pregnant woman.\n2. **Eugenic**: Substantial risk that the child, if born, would suffer from serious physical or mental abnormalities.\n3. **Humanitarian**: Pregnancy caused by rape or incest.\n4. **Social**: Failure of any contraceptive device or method used by a woman or her partner (applies to both married and unmarried women).\n\n### Differentiating Live Born from Dead Born\nA *live born* child is one that showed signs of life (breathing, heartbeat, cord pulsation, voluntary movement) after complete birth. A *dead born* (stillborn or dead before birth) child shows no signs of life.\n\n| Feature | Live Born | Dead Born (Stillborn) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Chest Cavity** | Expanded, arched, ribs are horizontal. | Flat, collapsed, ribs are oblique. |\n| **Lungs** | Voluminous, cover the heart, spongy, crepitant, pale pink. | Small, behind the heart, firm, liver-like (hepatized), dark red. |\n| **Hydrostatic Test** | Positive (lungs float in water). | Negative (lungs sink in water). |\n| **Stomach & Intestines** | Contain air (Breslau's test positive) and ingested milk. | Contain no air (sink in water), only meconium. |\n| **Umbilical Cord** | Shows drying, shriveling, and a line of demarcation (starts in 24 hrs). | No vital changes or line of demarcation; may show maceration. |\n| **Middle Ear** | Contains air (Wrede's test positive). | Contains embryonic gelatinous tissue (no air). |",
