    "text": "Hasse's Rule.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Infanticide & Child Abuse",
    "answer": "### Definition and Purpose\nHasse's Rule is a mathematical formula used in forensic medicine to estimate the gestational age of a fetus in intrauterine (lunar) months based on its crown-heel length.\n\n### The Rule\n- **For the First 5 Months of Gestation**:\n  The gestational age (in lunar months) is equal to the square root of the crown-heel length of the fetus in centimeters.\n  $$\\text{Gestational Age (months)} = \\sqrt{\\text{Length (cm)}}$$\n  *(Example: A length of 16 cm indicates a 4-month-old fetus).*\n\n- **For the Last 5 Months (6th to 10th Month) of Gestation**:\n  The gestational age (in lunar months) is equal to the crown-heel length of the fetus in centimeters divided by 5.\n  $$\\text{Gestational Age (months)} = \\frac{\\text{Length (cm)}}{5}$$\n  *(Example: A length of 40 cm indicates an 8-month-old fetus).*\n\n### Forensic Significance\nIt provides a rapid, reliable estimation of fetal age during autopsy or clinical examinations of aborted fetuses.",
