    "id": 204,
    "text": "NARCO ANALYSIS (Truth Serum Drugs)  -3 m",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Trace Evidence & Forensic Science",
    "answer": "### Definition\nNarco Analysis is a diagnostic psychobehavioral technique used in forensic investigation to extract truthful information from a suspect under the influence of sub-anesthetic doses of hypnotic drugs (popularly called \"truth serums\").\n\n### Drugs Used\nFast-acting barbiturates, primarily **Sodium Pentothal** (thiopentone sodium) or **Sodium Amytal**.\n\n### Mechanism\nThese drugs depress the central nervous system, lowering inhibitions and conscious control, making it difficult for the subject to fabricate lies. The subject enters a semi-conscious, hypnotic state (twilight sleep) where they answer questions freely.\n\n### Medico-legal Status\nIn India, the Supreme Court in the *Selvi vs. State of Karnataka* (2010) case ruled that involuntary administration of narco-analysis violates Article 20(3) (right against self-incrimination) and Article 21 (right to privacy) of the Constitution. It can only be performed with the voluntary consent of the subject.",
    "stars": 3
