    "answer": "### Overview\nDNA profiling (DNA fingerprinting) is a highly reliable molecular biological technique used in forensic science and toxicology.\n\n### Key Applications\n1. **Paternity and Maternity Testing**: To resolve civil disputes regarding child custody, inheritance, or disputed parentage.\n2. **Criminal Investigations**: To identify perpetrators of violent crimes like rape, murder, and physical assaults by matching suspect DNA with biological evidence (semen, blood, hair, saliva) found at the crime scene.\n3. **Identification of Mass Disaster Victims**: Identifying highly decomposed, mutilated, or skeletal remains in plane crashes, explosions, or natural disasters.\n4. **Immigration and Human Trafficking**: Verifying family relationships in immigration claims or identifying trafficked children.\n5. **Exoneration of the Innocent**: Re-evaluating past convictions using modern DNA analysis of preserved evidence.",
