    "text": "Poison Information Centre.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "General Toxicology",
    "answer": "### Definition\nA Poison Information Centre (PIC) is a specialized, 24/7 telephonic and digital information service designed to assist healthcare professionals and the general public in the rapid diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of poisoning.\n\n### Core Functions\n1. **Expert Consultation**: Providing immediate clinical guidance on toxic ingredients, lethal doses, treatment protocols, and specific antidotes.\n2. **Database Maintenance**: Maintaining a comprehensive, updated registry of commercial products, agricultural pesticides, household chemicals, and their toxic constituents.\n3. **Epidemiological Surveillance**: Tracking poisoning trends, toxic hazards, and outbreaks in the region.\n4. **Public Education**: Raising awareness about safe chemical storage, first aid, and poisoning prevention.\n\n### Importance\nPICs significantly reduce unnecessary hospitalizations by advising on non-toxic ingestions and optimize clinical outcomes in severe cases by facilitating rapid antidote administration.",
