    "text": "Toxicology vs Toxinology.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "General Toxicology",
    "answer": "### Toxicology\n- **Definition**: The broader scientific discipline that deals with the study of the physical, chemical, and biological properties of all poisons, their detection, clinical features, mechanisms of action, treatment, and legal regulations.\n- **Scope**: Encompasses synthetic chemicals, household products, industrial toxins, agricultural pesticides, drugs, and environmental pollutants.\n\n### Toxinology\n- **Definition**: A specialized subdiscipline of toxicology that specifically deals with the study of **biological toxins** produced by, or accumulated in, living organisms (animals, plants, fungi, and microbes).\n- **Scope**: Focuses on snake venom, scorpion venoms, bacterial toxins (botulinum, tetanus), mushroom toxins (amatoxins), and marine toxins.\n\n### Core Difference\nToxicology studies both synthetic/chemical and natural poisons, whereas Toxinology focuses exclusively on natural poisons (toxins) produced by living organisms.",
