    "id": 247,
    "text": "Add A Note On Mickey Finn/ Knockout Drops.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "CNS Depressants",
    "answer": "### Definition & Terminology\nA **Mickey Finn** (also known as **knockout drops**) is a slang term for a drink surreptitiously adulterated with a rapid-acting sedative-hypnotic or stupefying agent. It is administered to an unsuspecting individual to quickly render them unconscious or incapacitated, usually to facilitate crimes like robbery or sexual assault.\n\n### Composition\nHistorically, a Mickey Finn consisted of **chloral hydrate** mixed with alcohol. Chloral hydrate is rapidly metabolized in the body to trichloroethanol. When combined with alcohol, it produces a powerful, synergistic CNS depressant effect, leading to rapid onset of deep sleep. In modern times, liquid ecstasy (**GHB - gamma-hydroxybutyrate**), ketamine, or fast-acting benzodiazepines (like **flunitrazepam / Rohypnol** and midazolam) are commonly used.\n\n### Medico-Legal Importance (MLI)\nAdministering such stupefying agents with criminal intent is a serious offense under **Section 328 IPC (Section 112 BNS)**, which carries a punishment of up to 10 years imprisonment. The doctor must collect gastric lavage, blood, and urine samples to test for these sedative agents in suspected cases.",
