    "text": "Write About War Gases.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Asphyxiants",
    "answer": "### Definition\n**War gases** (or chemical warfare agents) are toxic chemical substances designed for military operations or terrorist activities to kill, seriously injure, or incapacitate enemy forces and populations.\n\n### Classification & Examples\n1. **Lacrymators (Tear Gases):** CN (chloroacetophenone) and CS gas. They cause severe ocular pain, burning, and involuntary blepharospasm.\n2. **Vesicants (Blister Agents):** Mustard gas and Lewisite. They cause severe, painful chemical burns and blistering of the skin and respiratory tract.\n3. **Asphyxiants (Choking Agents):** Chlorine and Phosgene. They damage alveolar membranes, leading to acute pulmonary edema and suffocation.\n4. **Blood/Systemic Agents:** Hydrogen cyanide. Inhibits cytochrome oxidase, halting cellular respiration.\n5. **Nerve Agents:** Sarin, Soman, Tabun, and VX. These are highly potent organophosphates that irreversibly inhibit acetylcholinesterase, leading to a fatal cholinergic crisis (bronchoconstriction, convulsions, and respiratory failure).\n\n### Medico-Legal Aspect\nThe use and stockpiling of chemical weapons are globally prohibited under the **Chemical Weapons Convention (CWC)**. They remain significant security concerns due to the threat of asymmetric warfare and domestic bioterrorism.",
