    "text": "Drug Dependence And Drug Abuse.",
    "type": "VSAQ",
    "chapter": "Pharmacological Toxicology & Food Poisoning",
    "answer": "### Definitions\n* **Drug Abuse:** The self-administration of any drug in a manner that deviates from established medical, social, or legal standards, resulting in physical, psychological, or social harm to the user or to society.\n* **Drug Dependence:** A state (psychological, physical, or both) arising from the repeated administration of a drug on a periodic or continuous basis. It is characterized by an overpowering compulsion to continue taking the drug.\n\n### Types of Dependence\n1. **Psychological Dependence:** An intense mental craving and compulsion to consume the drug to obtain pleasure, euphoria, or to avoid psychological discomfort (e.g., cannabis, cocaine).\n2. **Physical Dependence:** An altered physiological state where the body requires the continuous presence of the drug to function normally. Abrupt cessation of the drug triggers a specific, highly distressing **withdrawal syndrome** (e.g., opioids, alcohol, barbiturates).\n\n### Medico-Legal Importance\nUnder the **Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances (NDPS) Act** in India, the unauthorized possession, cultivation, sale, and consumption of dependence-producing drugs are severe criminal offenses carrying strict penalties.",
